---
/**
 * Copyright (DMCA) policy for soot and The Wired's servers: how to send a
 * notice under 17 U.S.C. §512(c)(3), how to counter-notice, and the
 * repeat-infringer policy the safe harbor requires (§512(i)).
 *
 * DRAFT — not legal advice. Counsel must review before publication. The
 * operator and the takedown inbox come from the app's legal text via
 * legal.json. The designated agent is registered with the US Copyright
 * Office; §512(c)(2) also wants the agent's name, address and phone on the
 * site, so fill AGENT in from the filed record and keep the two the same.
 */
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import legal from "../data/legal.json";

const UPDATED = "2026-10-06";
const operator = legal.operator.name;
const contact = Object.fromEntries(legal.contacts.map((c) => [c.kind, c.address]));

/** The designated agent as filed with the Copyright Office. Leave a field
 *  null until the filed value is known; the page says where to find it. */
const AGENT: { name: string | null; address: string[] | null; phone: string | null } = {
  name: null,
  address: null,
  phone: null,
};
const DIRECTORY = "https://dmca.copyright.gov/osp/";
const complete = AGENT.name && AGENT.address && AGENT.phone;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="copyright policy"
  description="How to report copyright infringement on soot, how to send a counter-notice, and what happens to repeat infringers."
  path="/dmca"
  updated={UPDATED}
>
  <section>
    <p>
      To report something on soot that infringes your copyright, write to{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.copyright}`}>{contact.copyright}</a>. An emailed notice that contains everything
      listed under "sending a notice" is effective. Notices are read by a person and answered within 24 hours.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>what this covers</h2>
    <p>
      {operator} ("we") runs the soot app and its default servers at thewired.app. We respect other people's
      rights and follow the Digital Millennium Copyright Act, 17 U.S.C. §512. This page says how to send a notice
      of claimed infringement, how to answer one if your upload was removed, and what we do about people who
      infringe repeatedly.
    </p>
    <p>
      soot is a client for Nostr, an open network. We can remove content from our own servers; we cannot remove
      copies held by relays that other people run. A notice to us covers what our servers carry.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>designated agent</h2>
    <p>
      Service provider: {operator}, also doing business as soot and The Wired, at thewired.app, soot.win and
      getsoot.app.
    </p>
    {AGENT.name && <p>Agent: {AGENT.name}</p>}
    {AGENT.address && (
      <p>
        {AGENT.address.map((line, i) => (
          <>
            {i > 0 && <br />}
            {line}
          </>
        ))}
      </p>
    )}
    {AGENT.phone && <p>Phone: {AGENT.phone}</p>}
    <p>
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${contact.copyright}`}>{contact.copyright}</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      The agent is registered in the US Copyright Office's{" "}
      <a href={DIRECTORY} rel="noopener">DMCA designated agent directory</a>, where the record can be found by searching
      for "{operator}".
      {!complete && " The record carries the agent's mailing address and phone, which will be added to this page."}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>sending a notice</h2>
    <p>For your notice to be effective under §512(c)(3) it must include all of the following:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your physical or electronic signature, as the owner of the copyright or someone authorised to act for them;</li>
      <li>which copyrighted work you say has been infringed, or a representative list if there are several;</li>
      <li>
        where the material is on soot, with enough detail for us to find it: a link, or the track and artist name,
        or the account that posted it;
      </li>
      <li>your name, address, telephone number and email address;</li>
      <li>
        a statement that you believe in good faith that the use is not authorised by the copyright owner, their
        agent or the law;
      </li>
      <li>
        a statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information in the notice is accurate and that you are the
        copyright owner or are authorised to act for them.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      When we receive a complete notice we remove or disable access to the material on our servers and tell the
      person who posted it, passing on your notice. Knowingly misrepresenting that something infringes carries
      liability under §512(f), including for costs and legal fees.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>counter-notice</h2>
    <p>
      If your upload was removed and you believe that was a mistake or that it was misidentified, you can send a
      counter-notice under §512(g)(3) to the same address. It must include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>your physical or electronic signature;</li>
      <li>what was removed and where it appeared before it was removed;</li>
      <li>
        a statement, under penalty of perjury, that you believe in good faith the material was removed by mistake
        or misidentification;
      </li>
      <li>
        your name, address and telephone number, a statement that you consent to the jurisdiction of the federal
        district court for the district where your address is (or, if you are outside the United States, any
        district in which we may be found), and that you will accept service of process from the person who sent the
        original notice.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We pass a complete counter-notice to the person who made the claim. Unless they tell us within 10 business
      days that they have gone to court to keep the material down, we restore it within 10 to 14 business days of
      receiving your counter-notice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>repeat infringers</h2>
    <p>
      Each valid notice counts against the account that posted the material. The first time, the material comes
      off our servers and the account is warned. An account that infringes repeatedly is removed from our servers,
      and may be removed sooner where the circumstances call for it. A removal that is reversed by a counter-notice
      does not count, and neither does a notice that is clearly defective.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>other complaints</h2>
    <p>
      This page is about copyright only. For trademark, impersonation or other complaints, write to{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.abuse}`}>{contact.abuse}</a>. For anything else:{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.support}`}>{contact.support}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
